      "status": "fixed",
      "status_notes": "wsgiref.headers.Headers accepted header names and values containing newline or other control characters, so user-controlled input could inject HTTP headers. Upstream fixed it in https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/143916 (3.13 commit https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/22e4d55285cee52bc4dbe061324e5f30bd4dee58), first released in CPython 3.13.12; see https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-0865, which lists 3.13 releases before 3.13.12 as affected. The later 3.13 change https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/83ecd18779f286d872f68bfce175651e407d9fff, first released in 3.13.13, only relaxes that check so that horizontal tabs are allowed in header values; it is not part of the fix. Compared Lib/wsgiref/headers.py in every published build of the DHI Alpine 3.23 python-3.13 package on x86_64 and aarch64 (3.13.12-r0 to 3.13.18-r4) with the upstream releases: 3.13.12-r0 and 3.13.12-r1 ship the upstream 3.13.12 file, which has the fix, and later builds ship the upstream 3.13.13 file, which also allows horizontal tabs in values. Every published build carries the fix, so the range's fixed version is the lowest published build."
    },
