      "status": "fixed",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-0865: wsgiref.headers.Headers accepted user-controlled header names and values containing newlines, allowing HTTP header injection. Upstream fixed it in https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/143916 (3.14 commit https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/23e3c0ae867cca0130e441e776c9955b9027c510), first released in CPython 3.14.3, which the CVE record lists as the first unaffected 3.14 release; see https://mail.python.org/archives/list/security-announce@python.org/thread/BJ6QPHNSHJTS3A7CFV6IBMCAP2DWRVNT/. A later 3.14.4 change (https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/bfba660085767f8c2d582134e9d511a85eda04cf) only allows a horizontal tab in header values again; https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-0865. Compared Lib/wsgiref/headers.py in every published build, 3.14.3-r0 to 3.14.10-r4, of the DHI Alpine 3.23 python-3.14 package on x86_64 and aarch64 with the files in the upstream CPython 3.14 releases. Every published build carries the fix; 3.14.3-r0 is the lowest published build."
